      "title": "New major risk - Financial position",
      "body": "The company's interest payments are not well covered by earnings. Net interest cover: 2.7x This is considered a major risk. If the company is unable to fund interest repayments on its debt through profits, it may be forced into reducing its debt burden through selling assets, undertaking a potentially costly capital raising or even into bankruptcy in the worst case scenario. Currently, the following risks have been identified for the company: Major Risks Interest payments are not well covered by earnings (2.7x net interest cover). High level of non-cash earnings (48% accrual ratio). Minor Risks Profit margins are more than 30% lower than last year (4.3% net profit margin). Market cap is less than US$100m (₹2.44b market cap, or US$25.7m).",
